Reflected Gray code for 3 bits:

```text
2 bits:  00 01 11 10
reverse: 10 11 01 00   → set bit 2 → 110 111 101 100
3 bits:  000 001 011 010 110 111 101 100   (0 1 3 2 6 7 5 4)
```

Maximum XOR in `[3, 10, 5, 25, 2, 8]`: the top bit (16) can be 1 (25 against anything below 16); then 8 (25 ^ 5 has it), then 4 — giving 11100 = 28 from 5 ^ 25.

